#NEXUS

[ li2011a_fig2: Sauropod time tree, root at the bottom. Each clade name is printed just right of the stem (or under the horizontal) of the node it names: SAUROPODA, EUSAUROPODA, NEOSAUROPODA, MACRONARIA and TITANOSAURIFORMES are kept as internal labels; TITANOSAURIFORMES sits between the Camarasaurus and Brachiosaurus nodes and is placed on the latter, since Camarasaurus is outside it in the drawing. One three-way node: Tonganosaurus, Omcisaurus and Mamenchisaurus, stem entering at Omcisaurus. 13 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children); 5 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 4 case (census 2, seed 20261201). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=13;
    TAXLABELS
        PROSAUROPODA
        Volcanodon
        Shunosaurus
        Barapasaurus
        Tonganosaurus
        Omcisaurus
        Mamenchisaurus
        Diplodocus
        Haplocanthosaurus
        Camarasaurus
        Brachiosaurus
        Euhelopus
        Titanosarus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE li2011a_fig2 = [&R] (PROSAUROPODA,(Volcanodon,(Shunosaurus,(Barapasaurus,((Tonganosaurus,Omcisaurus,Mamenchisaurus),(Diplodocus,(Haplocanthosaurus,(Camarasaurus,(Brachiosaurus,(Euhelopus,Titanosarus))TITANOSAURIFORMES))MACRONARIA)NEOSAUROPODA)))EUSAUROPODA)SAUROPODA);
END;
